\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 Everything he tried to salve his rage was like more oil on a fire. Or, if not oil, petrol. Or, if not petrol, then another three strikes of his Point of Order. Halo\'92s weapon was getting quite the polishing of late from perfectly timed strikes. He was in the prime of his art.\
He\'92d honed it: in one smooth motion, up and in, the three-edged spike slipping through flesh with surgical indifference, never glancing off the mandible, always finding that pulsing channel where blood pressure was highest. When the Point of Order hit just under the jaw, upward and inward at the carotid, orgasm and arterial spasm would produce a shower of blood in a brief, ecstatic arc, scarlet across his chest, the sheets, the wall. The wound a coroner might describe as three clean edges, one perfect jet.\
But not even three new murders could convince the dullard Commissioner of Traffic Movement and Property Security Incorporated, or Halo's own Bureau of Preemptive Reciprocity and Proactive Euthanasia (affectionately known as PAPER), to stop liking Chanta for the serial killings. If there was a concept Halo hated more than getting caught, it was someone else getting credit for his mayhem.\
But more galling: Chanta, after eight Halo-soaked years of being befriended and protected from unexplained accidents, poisonings, and sporting pursuits (white-water rafting in a river laced with barbed wire), was now being held by authorities even more incompetent than usual. Clearly, the people \'93in the know\'94\'97a cartel Halo had yet to even identify\'97had given up and just pinned everything on Chanta, the only man Halo knew who couldn't even kill a mood.\
Halo was incensed. And maybe, a little guilty. He\'92d failed to protect Chanta. Maybe he\'92d grown complacent, or distracted, certainly more interested in his own hunt at the Stickett Inn. Avi Grubler, the PAPER agent with the taste for detonations, had stolen his focus exactly when the bomb went off. \'93I come so hard when I blow things up,\'94 she\'92d said, or something like that, all glee and hunger. He should have made her talk, but instead settled for stopping her heart. Thinking back, she might have even revealed Chanta as her target, not that it much changed the numbers. Chanta was always the most valuable asset in any room, at least until Sarah walked in. Avi had no idea about her.\
That was why Halo was doubly incensed about Chanta being framed. He needed Chanta to lead the way to Sarah.\
None of this fit Halo\'92s solipsistic worldview, and the dissonance generated volumes of electric angst in his body, an itch that only violence could calm. He needed a new direction. Serial killing was getting dull. Time to turn his prodigious talents toward his other hobbies: political assassination and, when things were slow, lawn bowls.\
Why lawn bowls? Halo liked the shoes. The hats. He liked the smell of fresh-cut grass, almost as much as the smell of fresh-cut humanity. Bowls offered something restorative, unlike his brief foray into knitting. The needles reminded him too much of stabbing and the yarn too much of garrotting. Even the fluffiest mittens had proved a gateway drug back to recreational murder. Lawn bowls, by contrast, led at worst to vigorous disagreements about scorekeeping with opponents too medicated to register proper terror\
And political assassination: the newly minted Commissioner richly deserved being a target. Not only did he cut across everything Halo wanted, he was a personal stooge for the CEO of Ulyssia, another seat-filler from the Prosperity Mountain Church of Exclusive Faith. Halo loathed the sanctimonious kind.\
Killing the Commissioner was the easy part\'97Halo had PAPER's tools and training. Disposing of the corpse creatively, that was the satisfaction. This one was almost art: Commissioner\'92s body, dog food factory, batch traced, the ten ugliest local strays feasted for a fortnight, their faeces collected and stuffed into effigies dressed in white-supremacist garb, tied to stakes, and burned on the lawns of Prosperity Mountain Church\'92s headquarters.\
Halo considered it a restorative holiday.\
